.TH "CSSTRANSFORMVALUE.CSSTRANSFORMVALUE" "3JS" "September 10, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSTransformValue.CSSTransformValue \- CSSTransformValue:
CSSTransformValue() constructor
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]CSSTransformValue()\f[B]\f[R] constructor creates a new
\f[CR]CSSTransformValue\f[R] object, representing a
\f[CR]transform\-list\f[R] value made up of the given
\f[CR]CSSTransformComponent\f[R] objects.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
new CSSTransformValue(transforms)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]transforms\f[R]
An array of \f[CR]CSSTransformComponent\f[R] objects.
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]TypeError\f[R]
Thrown if \f[CR]transforms\f[R] is empty.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] transform = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSTransformValue([
  \f[B]new\f[R] CSSTranslate(CSS.px(10), CSS.px(20)),
  \f[B]new\f[R] CSSScale(2, 3),
]);

console.log(transform.length); \f[I]// 2\f[R]
console.log(transform.toString()); \f[I]// \(dqtranslate(10px, 20px) scale(2, 3)\(dq\f[R]
.EE
.SS Handling an empty array
The constructor throws a \f[CR]TypeError\f[R] if \f[CR]transforms\f[R]
is empty:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]try\f[R] {
  \f[B]const\f[R] transform = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSTransformValue([]);
} \f[B]catch\f[R] (e) {
  console.log(e); \f[I]// TypeError\f[R]
}
.EE
